---
/**
 * /en/cookie-policy/ — tradução fiel de /politica-de-cookies/ (texto
 * definitivo do escritório, versão 1.0, vigente a partir de 11/09/2026).
 * Manter sincronizada com src/pages/politica-de-cookies.astro: qualquer
 * mudança de conteúdo lá precisa ser feita aqui também. Em caso de
 * divergência, vale o texto em português.
 *
 * Os ids das seções são os mesmos da versão em português: o banner
 * (AvisoCookies.astro) aponta para `#cookies-utilizados` nos dois idiomas.
 */
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import '~/styles/politica.css';

const secoes = [
  { id: 'o-que-sao', rotulo: 'What cookies are' },
  { id: 'categorias', rotulo: 'Categories we use' },
  { id: 'gerenciar', rotulo: 'How to manage your choices' },
  { id: 'cookies-utilizados', rotulo: 'Cookies used' },
  { id: 'transferencia', rotulo: 'International transfer' },
];
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  alternativa="/politica-de-cookies/"
  sobreposto={false}
  titulo="Cookie Policy | Bertoncini & Mendonça Advogados"
  descricao="Cookie Policy of Bertoncini & Mendonça Advogados: what cookies are, the categories we use, how to manage your choices and the cookies used on the website."
>
  <article class="politica">
    <div class="env">
      <p class="chapeu">Legal document</p>
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="atualizado">Version 1.0, effective from November 18, 2026</p>

      <div class="texto">
        <p>
          Our website always uses necessary cookies and uses the others only with your
          permission, which can be given or withdrawn at any time through the
          “<button type="button" class="abrir-preferencias" data-abrir-cookies>Cookie preferences</button>”
          link in the footer of every page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <nav class="sumario" aria-label="Sections of this policy">
        <h2>On this page</h2>
        <ol>
          {secoes.map((secao) => (
            <li><a href={`#${secao.id}`}>{secao.rotulo}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="texto">
        <h2 id="o-que-sao">What cookies are</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files stored in your browser when you visit a
          website. They allow the website to work, to remember your choices and, if
          you allow it, to generate statistics and measure ads. We also use the term
          for similar technologies, such as pixels and local storage. First-party
          cookies are set by our website; third-party cookies, by other companies
          whose services we use. Some last only while the browser is open (session
          cookies); others remain for the period shown in the table (persistent
          cookies).
        </p>

        <h2 id="categorias">Categories we use</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Necessary (always active).</strong> They ensure that the website
          works and is secure, and they store your choices about cookies. Without them
          the website does not work as it should. Legal basis: legitimate interest.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Analytics (subject to your permission).</strong> We use Google
          Analytics, through Google Tag Manager, to find out how many people visit the
          website, which pages are read the most and where visits come from. The
          reports are aggregated and we do not use this information to identify you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Advertising and measurement (subject to your permission).</strong> We
          use the Meta Pixel, the Google Ads tag and the LinkedIn Insight Tag to measure
          the results of our institutional ads and to show them to people who have
          already visited the website. These companies may associate this data with
          your account on their platforms, in accordance with their respective
          policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Third-party content (subject to your permission).</strong> YouTube
          videos and Instagram and LinkedIn posts embedded in the website are only
          loaded after you give permission; until then, a notice appears with the
          option to load the content. The WhatsApp button is a simple link and does
          not store cookies on our website; when you click it, you are taken to
          WhatsApp, a Meta service.
        </p>

        <h2 id="gerenciar">How to manage your choices</h2>
        <p>
          On your first visit, a banner lets you accept all cookies, reject
          non-essential cookies or choose by category, with equal prominence for each
          option. Withdrawing your permission is as easy as giving it: just click
          “<button type="button" class="abrir-preferencias" data-abrir-cookies>Cookie preferences</button>”
          in the footer. You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings
          (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari or another), bearing in mind that blocking
          necessary cookies may affect how the website works.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cookies-utilizados">Cookies used</h2>
        {/*
          A tabela veio VAZIA no documento do cliente. As três primeiras linhas
          são o que o site grava hoje; as demais são as ferramentas citadas,
          ainda não instaladas.
        */}
        <div class="tabela">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Cookie</th>
                <th scope="col">Provider</th>
                <th scope="col">Category</th>
                <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col">Duration</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>consentimento</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">Bertoncini & Mendonça Advogados (first party)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Necessary</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Store your choices about cookies</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">12 months (local storage)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>bm-a11y</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">Bertoncini & Mendonça Advogados (first party)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Necessary</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Store the accessibility settings you choose (text size, contrast, underlined links)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">Persistent, until you clear the website’s data in your browser (local storage)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>bm-entrada</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">Bertoncini & Mendonça Advogados (first party)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Necessary</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Remember that the opening animation has already been shown, so it is not repeated on every page</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">Session (session storage)</td>
              </tr>
              {/*
                CONFERIR QUANDO AS TAGS FOREM INSTALADAS: cookies padrão de Google
                Analytics, Google Ads, Pixel da Meta e LinkedIn Insight Tag. Hoje
                nenhuma dessas tags está no site. Ver o comentário na versão em
                português.
              */}
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>_ga</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">Google (Google Analytics)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Analytics</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Distinguish visitors to generate aggregated website usage statistics</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">2 years</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">Google (Google Analytics)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Analytics</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Keep the session state for website usage statistics</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">2 years</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>_gcl_au</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">Google (Google Ads)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Advertising and measurement</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Measure the results (conversions) of Google Ads ads</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">3 months</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>_fbp</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">Meta (Meta Pixel)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Advertising and measurement</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Identify the browser to measure Meta ads and show them to people who have already visited the website</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">3 months</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>li_sugr</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">LinkedIn (LinkedIn Insight Tag)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Advertising and measurement</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Identify the browser to measure LinkedIn ads</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">3 months</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>bcookie</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">LinkedIn (LinkedIn Insight Tag)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Advertising and measurement</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Identify the browser accessing LinkedIn services</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">1 year</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>lidc</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">LinkedIn (LinkedIn Insight Tag)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Advertising and measurement</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Select the LinkedIn server (data center) that serves the browser</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">24 hours</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>UserMatchHistory</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">LinkedIn (LinkedIn Insight Tag)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Advertising and measurement</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Sync identifiers to show LinkedIn ads to people who have already visited the website</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><code>AnalyticsSyncHistory</code></th>
                <td data-rotulo="Provider">LinkedIn (LinkedIn Insight Tag)</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Category">Advertising and measurement</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Purpose">Record when the UserMatchHistory cookie was last synced</td>
                <td data-rotulo="Duration">30 days</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 id="transferencia">International transfer</h2>
        <p>
          Google, Meta and LinkedIn may process the data collected by these cookies on
          servers outside Brazil, mainly in the United States. When you authorize
          these categories, you are informed in advance of this international nature,
          as provided for in art. 33, VIII, of the LGPD (Brazil’s General Personal Data
          Protection Law). The other points about the processing of your data are in
          the <a href="/en/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
